{
  "_synthetic": "Made up, in the shape of the chat service's answers to POST v1/agents/28:<bot>/invoke (docs/protocol/bots.md), every value made up. Seen in the lab's Workflows runs of 2026-11-05: HTTP 200 with the envelope {\"responseType\": <kind>, <kind>: ...} for commands (composeExtension type command), a dialog (task type continue with an Adaptive Card), the just-in-time install dialog (installDialog: the app asks to be added first, its Submit data carrying msteams.justInTimeInstall; seen in the Approvals run of 2026-11-16), and HTTP 200 with an empty text/plain body (done: a submitAction, or an app with no commands). The others follow the public Teams and Bot Framework documentation in the same envelope and are unseen: results (composeExtension type result), message (composeExtension type message), taskMessage (task type message), and the universal action responses of adaptiveCard/action (card, executeMessage, error, signIn).",
